Third-party data

The sample data under dev/taihei/mihon/data/ was derived from the sources
below by the scripts in scripts/data/. docs/data-sources.md records the
versions, download dates and processing of each.

Unicode CLDR 47 (country names, quotation marks, likely subtags) and the
Unicode Han Database, Unihan 16.0.0 (Mandarin readings).
Copyright (c) 2004-2025 Unicode, Inc. Distributed under the Unicode
License v3; the full text is in LICENSE-UNICODE.

Word frequencies derived from sentences of the Tatoeba Project
(https://tatoeba.org), written by the Tatoeba contributors and licensed
under CC BY 2.0 FR (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/).
Only single words, filtered, with weights computed from their counts are
included. No sentence is reproduced.

Address formats and postal code patterns are written for this library,
based on the address metadata of Google libaddressinput
(https://github.com/google/libaddressinput), licensed under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). They were adapted and
changed.

Given names, family names, cities, region names and Latin country names
from Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org), dedicated to the public domain
under CC0 1.0.

United States given names (1990) and surnames (2010) from the U.S. Census
Bureau, a work of the United States Government not protected by copyright
